-          "quote": "Let $Q\\subseteq\\mathbb R^d$ be open and star-shaped about a point $q_*\\in Q$, meaning $q_*+t(q-q_*)\\in Q$ for every $q\\in Q$ and $t\\in[0,1]$. Let $M$ be real symmetric positive-definite, $U=Q\\times\\mathbb R^d$, and $H(q,p)=\\tfrac12p^TM^{-1}p+V(q)$ with $V\\in C^\\infty(Q)$. Let $\\Phi_h$ be the kick-then-drift symplectic-Euler map, the local leapfrog map, or an admitted implicit-midpoint branch, on a compact subset where the chosen map is defined. Write $r=1$ for the kick-then-drift symplectic-Euler map and $r=2$ for leapfrog or implicit midpoint, as proved in [[thm-local-symplectic-euler-and-leapfrog-trajectory-errors]] and [[thm-implicit-midpoint-branch-symplectic-order-and-error]]. For a smooth test function $f$, define the pullback $P_hf=f\\circ\\Phi_h$ by its Taylor coefficients at $h=0$. For fixed finite $N\\ge r$, its truncated logarithm is the polynomial\n$$\\log_N(P_h)=\\sum_{k=1}^{N+1}\\frac{(-1)^{k+1}}{k}(P_h-I)^k,$$\ncomputed modulo terms of order $h^{N+2}$. There are smooth vector fields $X_r,\\ldots,X_N$ and globally defined functions $H_r,\\ldots,H_N$ on $U$ such that\n$$h^{-1}\\log_N(P_h)=\\mathcal L_{X_H}+\\sum_{j=r}^Nh^j\\mathcal L_{X_j}\\pmod{h^{N+1}},\\qquad \\iota_{X_j}\\omega=dH_j,$$\nwhere $\\mathcal L_Xf:=Df[X]$. Thus $H_h^{[N]}=H+\\sum_{j=r}^Nh^jH_j$ is a globally defined finite modified Hamiltonian. The logarithm is a finite formal polynomial for each fixed $N$; no convergence of an infinite series is asserted.\n\n",
